Ok

After this day of observation im near 100% sure that this cpu load is=20
made by route cahce flushes
When route cache increase to its "net.ipv4.route.gc_thresh" size or is=20
near that size
system is starting to drop some routes from cache then cpu load is=20
increase from 2% to near 80%
after cleaning / flush cache when cache is filling cpu load is again=20
normal 2%

Someone know how to resolve this ?
on kernels < 2.6.29 i don't see this, all start after upgrade from=20
2.6.28 to 2.6.29 - then i try 2.6.29.1 , 2.6.29.3 and 2.6.30 and on all=
=20
this kernels >=3D 2.6.29 problem with cpu load is the same.

I can minimize this cpu fluctuations by changing of route cache /proc=20
parameters but the best result for my router was

15 sec of 2% cpu
and after
15sec of 80% cpu


